INTRODUCTION: 

What is SpringBoot??

Spring Boot is an open-Source java framework that makes it easy to create stand-alone, production-grade Spring based Applications that you can "just run".
																					   ________________
Health checks
Error Handling
Integrations - Security
Logging 
Configuration is easy.

What programmers do before SpringBoot??

Spring Boot is a popular Java framework that simplifies the process of creating stand-alone, production-ready Spring-based applications.
Before Spring Boot, developers had to manually configure and set up various components of the Spring framework, which could be time-consuming and complex. Spring Boot automates much of this configuration, allowing developers to focus on writing business logic and reducing development time.

--Traditional Java EE(Enterprise Edition) / Servlet-Based Approach.
--Developers used servlets and JDBC manually.
--Lots of boilerplate code.
--Hard to test, hard to maintain.
--Xml-based configurations(painful!).



JAR(Java Archive): Package Java Applications(Libraries/ Tools).
WAR(WebApp Archive): Package web Applications(Servlet/ JSP-based apps).

| Feature    | JAR                           | WAR                            |
| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Stands for | Java ARchive                  | Web Application ARchive        |
| Used for   | Libraries / tools / apps      | Web applications (JSP/Servlet) |
| Run with   | `java -jar`                   | Deployed on web server         |
| Contains   | `.class`, resources, META-INF | Web content + `WEB-INF` folder |
